UniFetch-API

This implementation incorporates adaptations of video parsing and Motion Photo
code from tidain/YunX-Desktop, licensed under GNU AGPL version 3.
Upstream repository: https://github.com/tidain/YunX-Desktop
Reference commit: 00a030f778a65840e9be65baecb15497a94b04ec

Adapted modules include DouyinParser.kt, XhsParser.kt, BilibiliParser.kt,
VideoLinkParser.kt, VideoModels.kt, VideoHttp.kt, MotionPhotoWriter.kt.
Local changes include Python translation, Chromium response capture, best video
selection, structured image/motion pairing, persistent HTTP jobs, authentication,
signed media downloads, Docker packaging and Shortcuts integration guidance.

The full license is supplied in LICENSE. Corresponding source for this running
version is downloadable at /source.tar.gz. The archive excludes runtime tokens,
platform cookies, user submissions and downloaded media.

This distribution also incorporates the X/Twitter guest GraphQL and media
normalization principles from FxEmbed/FxEmbed, licensed under the MIT License.
Vendored reference commit:
2e9097877863050749f7ab555ce0c77a8caa70b4. The upstream license and source are
included in vendor/fxembed/LICENSE.md and the /source.tar.gz archive. Local
changes include a Python implementation of the guest token/GraphQL request,
raw tweet media normalization, and highest-bitrate variant selection inside the
single UniFetch-API container.
